@* The one copy of the controls help. It shows under the start lamps, when it is needed, and in
   the pause menu, when it is asked for; the start card's "Controls" disclosure is gone. The
   stylesheet shows the line that matches the device (keys on a fine pointer, pedals on touch). *@
<p class="racer-controls">
    <span class="for-keys">W / ↑ gas · S / ↓ brake · A D / ← → steer · Space drift · Esc menu</span>
    <span class="for-touch">Hold the arrows and pedals at the bottom of the screen</span>
    <span class="for-pad">Gamepad: stick steers · RT gas · LT brake · X drift</span>
    <span class="for-tips">Hold Drift through a bend and let go for a boost · tuck in behind a car for a tow · arrows on the road are boost pads</span>
</p>
